\section{Astrophysics Integration Layer}

\subsection{Overview}
The astrophysics integration layer serves as the physical intake system for the
simulation engine. It merges external curvature, stress-energy, cosmological
behavior, and warp-field contributions into the unified blueprint architecture.
This layer ensures that the engine evolves according to physically grounded
constraints rather than arbitrary inputs.

\subsection{Governing Field Equation}
The integration layer is defined by the warp-augmented field equation:
\begin{equation}
\tilde{G}_{\mu\nu} + \Lambda g_{\mu\nu}
=
\frac{8\pi G}{c^4} T_{\mu\nu}
\oplus
\mathcal{J}_{\text{warp}},
\end{equation}
where $\tilde{G}_{\mu\nu}$ is the modified Einstein tensor, $\Lambda$ is the
cosmological constant, $T_{\mu\nu}$ is the stress-energy tensor, and
$\mathcal{J}_{\text{warp}}$ represents non-classical warp-field contributions.

\subsection{Curvature Ingestion}
External curvature fields are mapped into the blueprint geometry through:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{C}_{\text{curv}}
=
\nabla_{\alpha}
\left(
\Gamma^{\alpha}_{\;\mu\nu}
\right),
\end{equation}
providing the engine with real-time geometric structure.

\subsection{Stress-Energy Mapping}
The stress-energy tensor is merged with the unified energy-density invariant:
\begin{equation}
E_{\text{eff}}(R)
=
E_{\text{mass}}(R)
+
E_{\text{field}}(R)
+
E_{\text{stress}}(R),
\end{equation}
ensuring consistent horizon-free evolution under the constraint:
\begin{equation}
R > \frac{2G}{c^4} E_{\text{eff}}(R).
\end{equation}

\subsection{Warp-Field Augmentation}
Warp-field behavior enters through the augmentation term:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{J}_{\text{warp}}
=
\nabla_{\beta}
\left(
F^{\beta\mu}
+
\Omega^{\beta\mu}
\right),
\end{equation}
where $F^{\beta\mu}$ and $\Omega^{\beta\mu}$ represent field-strength and
geometric warp contributions.

\subsection{Integration into State-Space Evolution}
The astrophysics intake feeds directly into the state-space evolution equation:
\begin{equation}
\frac{d\Sigma}{dt}
=
\mathcal{C}_{\text{inv}}
+
\mathcal{S}_{\text{stab}}
+
\mathcal{D}_{\text{prevent}},
\end{equation}
ensuring that external physics is transformed into blueprint-governed behavior.

\subsection{Summary}
The astrophysics integration layer acts as the bridge between external physical
structure and the internal blueprint architecture. It merges curvature,
stress-energy, and warp-field contributions into a unified invariant framework,
allowing the simulation engine to evolve coherently and horizon-free.